\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 29\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 -33\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Robertus Grosseteste (?)}}\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Disputatio animae et corporis}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Incipit disputatio corporis et anime rithmice composita per magistrum Rubertum epicospum Linconiensem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 \u8249 \'8b {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Ecce mundus moritur viciis sepultus}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \u8230 \'85-\u8230 \'85 (29\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 hanc sequens retrahatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 . {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Vir quidam extiterat }}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 \u8230 \'85-\u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 et me Christi manibus totum commendavi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 . Schreibervers (33\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Det pater et filius et cum sancto flamen cum mea nos perducat amen.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 1481\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Finit disputatio animae et corporis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 . In der Hs gehen Carmen de miseria mundi (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , Initia Carminum 5114) und Visio Philiberti (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , Initia Carminum 20421) direkt ineinander \u252 \'fcber (insges. 368 Verse). Druck (carmen): AH 33 Nr. 242, S. 264 f.; (visio): \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22 T. Wright\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , The Latin Poems Commonly Attributed to Walter Mapes, London 1841 (ND Hildesheim 1968) S. 95-106. Zum Text: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22 H. Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , Streitgedicht S. 63-74, zur \u220 \'dcberlieferung (zu erg.) S. 211-214; zur umstrittenen\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Verfasserschaft:  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 VL 10, Sp. 412 ff. (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22 N.F. Palmer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , mit weiterer Lit.). Am Blattrand (29\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) Verse (Anleitung f\u252 \'fcr Illustration\~?): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Figura vite\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (es folgt Str. 12 des carmen); \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Figura mortis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Dic homo vas cinerum \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , Proverbia 5561a. }

